    "updated_at": "2025-10-09T12:49:11Z",
    "body": "One thing this would require specifically for popover is a new pseudo-class to match elements that are popovers. Currently UA styles use `[popover]` but that wouldn't work if we could enable it via element internals.\n\n`draggable` is also a presentational attribute at least in Chromium and presumably WebKit, it's used to set `-webkit-user-drag`. That makes it a bit trickier as it could lead to cycles if that property made the element match the pseudo-class too. So we'd need to make sure only the attribute presence *or* element internals usage made the pseudo-class match.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
