    "created_at": "2025-10-09T17:02:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-09T17:02:43Z",
    "body": "I'm curious about the use cases here. For example, all built-in elements need to have the `popover` attribute explicitly on the element for it to be a popover. The \"owner\" of the element is in charge of adding it to the element. If a custom element itself is to be a popover, it seems like it might be best if it behaves just like the built-ins, in that it requires an explicit attribute? If the custom element wants to *use* a popover, it can certainly add one within its shadow root directly. Is there a good use case example that might help me understand how this would be used?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
